# Aetherfield — the canonical list of environment variables.
#
# NAMES ONLY. Real values never land in this file or in the repository; they
# come from `vercel env pull .env.local`, which is gitignored (AGENTS.md 8.4).
#
# Every variable here is server-only. Phase one needs no `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at
# all, and adding one is a decision to make a value public.
#
# This file is extended by the build step that provisions each variable — never
# ahead of it, because the provider owns the name and it is read back from
# `vercel env ls` rather than guessed.

# --- Step 1: Neon Postgres (provisioned) -----------------------------------
# Pooled (PgBouncer, the `-pooler` host). What the application uses, and the
# only one `lib/db/client.ts` reads.
DATABASE_URL=
# Direct. What migrations, pg_dump, logical replication and LISTEN/NOTIFY
# require, and what `drizzle.config.ts` reads. The app never uses it.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# --- Step 2: Upstash Redis (provisioned) -----------------------------------
# The REST endpoint and its token, under the names the Upstash Marketplace
# integration actually sets — `KV_REST_API_*`, not the `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_*`
# that Upstash's own docs and `Redis.fromEnv()` expect. Read back from
# `vercel env ls`, not guessed. `lib/rate-limit/` reads them, lazily, so
# `next build` succeeds without them. Neither is NEXT_PUBLIC_*: a rate limiter
# whose token a browser can read is not a rate limiter.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# Also set by the integration and deliberately unused: KV_REST_API_READ_ONLY_TOKEN
# (a limiter counts, so it needs the write token), KV_URL and REDIS_URL (the
# TCP endpoints; the REST client is what runs on Fluid Compute).
# BotID (build step 2) needs no environment variable at all — the challenge is
# proxied through the app's own origin by `withBotId` in `next.config.ts`.

# --- Step 6: Better Auth ---------------------------------------------------
# Generated locally, at least 32 characters. Rotation uses
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS (plural), which is not configured until it is needed.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# The application's base URL. Server-only; callbacks resolve against it.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=
# Google OAuth Web application credentials. The configured redirect URI must
# be <BETTER_AUTH_URL>/api/auth/callback/google for each environment.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
